5.51 Local Subprogram (M97)
A local subprogram is a block of code in the main program that is referenced several times
by the main program. Local subprograms are commanded (called) using an M97 and
Pnnnnn, which refers to the N line number of the local subprogram.
The local subprogram format is to end the main program with an M30 then enter the local
subprograms after the M30. Each subprogram must have an N line number at the start and
a M99 at the end that will send the program back to the next line in the main program.
