5.54 External Subprograms With Multiple Fixtures 
(M98)
Subprograms can be useful when cutting the same part in different X and Y locations within
the machine. For example, there are six vises mounted on the table. Each of these vises
uses a new X, Y zero. They are referenced in the program using the G54 through G59 work
offsets in absolute coordinates. Use an edge finder or an indicator to establish the zero
point on each part. Use the part zero set key in the work offset page to record each X, Y
location. Once the X, Y zero position for each workpiece is in the offset page, the
programming can begin.
The figure shows what this setup would look like on the machine table. For an example,
each of these six parts will need to be drilled at the center, X and Y zero.
