8.1.42 M99 Subprogram Return or Loop
P - Program line number to go to when conditional test is met
M99 has three main uses:
• M99 is used at the end of a subprogram, local subprogram, or macro to return back
to the main program.
• An M99 Pnn jumps the program to the corresponding Nnn in the program.
• An M99 in the main program causes the program to loop back to the beginning and
execute until [RESET] is pressed.

